{title: Sing a New Song}
{subtitle: Psalms 98:1–3}
{key: D}
{tempo: 87}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | [D] | [D] | [D] |
| [D] | [G] | [G] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Sing to the LORD a new song
He has done great [G]wonders today
[Bm7]His right hand and holy [A]arm
Have won him victory in [G]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
The LORD has [Bm7]made his salvation [A]known
Revealed his [G]righteousness clear
Before the [Bm7]eyes of all nations
[A]His truth is now ap[G]pearing here
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing to the [D]LORD a new [A]song
[Bm7]Shout for joy to all the [G]earth
All the [D]ends have seen the [A]light
Salvation of our [G]God is worth
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]He has remembered his mercy
His faith[G]fulness to Israel
[Bm7]The whole world has seen the [A]way
His love is ful[G]ly revealed
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Pre-Chorus (repeat)}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Make music to the LORD with [D]lyre
With the [A]sound of sweet [Bm]song
With [G]trumpets and ram's horn [D]shout
Before the [A]King, the Lord
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Sing to the [D]LORD a new [A]song
His [G]victory is forever strong [D]
{end_of_verse}
